.TH CWE-434 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-434 \- Unrestricted Upload of File with Dangerous Type
.SH RANK
2025 CWE Top 25 rank: \fB#12\fR (2024 rank: 10).
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: Web / File Handling.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Uploads are accepted without adequately restricting the type or how the file is handled. An attacker uploads executable content (e.g. a web shell) into a location the server executes, achieving remote code execution.
.SH MITIGATION
Validate by content (not just extension); allow\-list permitted types; generate a server\-side random filename; store uploads outside the web root or where scripts never execute; serve with a safe Content\-Type/Content\-Disposition.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB24\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2017\-12615
Apache Tomcat, added 2022\-03\-25, ransomware: Known.
.PP
Apache Tomcat on Windows Remote Code Execution Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
When running Apache Tomcat on Windows with HTTP PUTs enabled, it is possible to upload a JSP file to the server via a specially crafted request. This JSP could then be requested and any code it contained would be executed by the server.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2022\-04\-15.
.PP
